  "published": "2026-10-09T07:36:03Z",
  "modified": "2026-10-09T07:36:03Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: credentials leaked to another origin on HTTP redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91766.patch: strip the Authorization, Cookie\n       and Proxy-Authorization user headers when a redirect changes the\n       scheme, host or port, and remove whole header lines in\n       ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c\n     - CVE-2026-91766\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-read in TLS wildcard certificate name\n     matching\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91767.patch: include the wildcard prefix\n       length in the subject length check so memchr() cannot read past the\n       peer name in ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c\n     - CVE-2026-91767\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: FastCGI allowed_clients matched IPv6 clients on a /96\n     prefix\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91768.patch: compare the full 16-byte IPv6\n       address in fcgi_is_allowed() in main/fastcgi.c\n     - CVE-2026-91768\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: TLS peer name check fell back to the certificate CN\n     when the certificate has a service identity\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91769.patch: do not fall back to the Common\n       Name when the certificate has a DNS, URI or SRV subjectAltName in\n       ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c\n     - CVE-2026-91769\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-read on an empty Location header in HTTP\n     redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-93682.patch: use the stored Location length\n       instead of strlen() and of reading the second byte when resolving a\n       relative redirect in ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c\n     - CVE-2026-93682",
